From: DuskyProjects <actions@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: usb: qcom: document multiplexed PHY selection

Document the board opt-in used on IPQ5332 systems where the DWC3
SuperSpeed pads share a TCSR-controlled mux with PCIe. The corresponding
driver support selects the USB path before the controller reset.

---
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/qcom,snps-dwc3.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/qcom,snps-dwc3.yaml
@@ -147,6 +147,13 @@ properties:
       HS/FS/LS modes are supported.
     type: boolean
 
+  qcom,multiplexed-phy:
+    description:
+      Select the USB side of the SoC-specific shared USB and PCIe PHY mux
+      before the DWC3 reset sequence. This property is used by IPQ5332 boards
+      whose SuperSpeed pads are multiplexed through TCSR.
+    type: boolean
+
   wakeup-source: true
 
 # Required child node:
